  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sales that were sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "That correction does not change the calculation. Faraday’s flower shop sold 50 bouquets, including 12 sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Noted. Individual sunflowers cost \\$3 each. To calculate the revenue from sunflower bouquets, we would also need to know how many individual sunflowers were in each bouquet.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday earns \\$26 per day from individual sunflowers. Over 3 days:\n\n\\[\n26 \\times 3 = \\$78\n\\]\n\nEach individual sunflower sells for \\$3, so:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{78}{3}=26\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nThe bouquet figures imply \\(56 \\div 8=7\\) bouquets per day, or 21 bouquets in three days, but the number of individual sunflowers inside those bouquets is not specified.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days, Faraday sold:\n\n- **Individual sunflowers:**  \n  \\[\n  \\$26 \\times 3=\\$78\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  \\$78\\div \\$3=26\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\n- **Bouquets:**  \n  \\[\n  \\$56\\div \\$8=7\\text{ bouquets per day}\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  7\\times 3=21\\text{ bouquets}\n  \\]\n  Each bouquet has 12 sunflowers:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Using the corrected price of **$2 per individual sunflower**:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$26 \\times 3}{\\$2}=\\frac{\\$78}{\\$2}=39\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}\\times 3=7\\times 3=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
